 "text": " To keep networking organized, engineers divide the job into four stack layers. First, the applications layers format data for your app, such as HTTP for webpages. Second, the transport layers build data into numbered segments and manage delivery using TCP or UDP. Third, the internet layers add IP addresses and routes packets across networks. works for the link layer move raw bits of a physical Wi-Fi radio waves copper Ethernet cables or fiber optics at the transport layer you have a crucial choice TCP or UDP TCP is like registered mail it takes every packet as the sender to retransmit anything lost and guarantees every byte arrives in order You need TCP for downloading code, banking or sending email where one missing byte corrupts the file. UDP skips the receive and retransmissions to send packets as fast as possible. You use UDP for live video calls or multiplayer games where waiting half a second for an old lost frame is worse than skipping straight to the newest frame.",
